            <ArticleTitle>A rare case of advanced ovarian carcinoma who developed difficulty walking 25 days after treatment with weekly paclitaxel.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>631-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although taxol has shown significant activity in advanced ovarian cancer, peripheral neuropathy is likely to become the major dose-limiting toxicity. We describe a case of advanced ovarian carcinoma who developed difficulty walking because of marked pain in the lower extremities and loss of proprioception 25 days after treatment with weekly taxol (80 mg/m(2)x3).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
